## FAQ

**Will a three-minute delay really stop me from eating?** Not every time. Some nights the urge fades, and some nights you'll still eat. What changes is that you're choosing after a pause, not during the first rush. Many people find that's a smaller, easier thing to practice than "never snack at night."

**What if I only get bored-hungry on certain nights?** Then use it on those nights only. There's no streak to protect. Keep the timer ready for the evenings you know are harder, like after a long day or a night with nothing planned.

**Can I use this for urges that aren't about food?** Yes. The same three-minute pause works for late-night online shopping, doomscrolling, or anything where your hand moves before you've decided. The steps are the same: stay put, start the timer, decide after.

